    "heading": "ecosystem-repositories",
    "content": "| Project    | Ecosystem              | Source Repository |\n| ---------- | ---------------------- | ----------------- |\n| **Python** | PyPI (uv, pip, poetry) | GitHub Repository |",
    "table": "table-0"
  }, {
    "heading": "ecosystem-repositories",
    "content": "| Project | Ecosystem            | Source Repository |\n| ------- | -------------------- | ----------------- |\n| **PHP** | Packagist (Composer) | GitHub Repository |",
    "table": "table-0"
  }, {
    "heading": "ecosystem-repositories",
    "content": "| Project                       | Ecosystem             | Source Repository |\n| ----------------------------- | --------------------- | ----------------- |\n| **Documentation & Converter** | Next.js 16 / Fumadocs | GitHub Repository |",
    "table": "table-0"
  }, {
    "heading": "core-contribution-principles",
    "content": "Before proposing changes, please keep our core architectural principles in mind:"
  }, {
    "heading": "core-contribution-principles",
    "content": "**Zero External Runtime Dependencies**:\nAll three language packages (`nepali-date-library`) MUST maintain zero external dependencies at runtime. Do not add runtime packages."
  }, {
    "heading": "core-contribution-principles",
    "content": "**Standardized Cross-Language Semantics**:\nThe API surface across Node.js, Python, and PHP is intentionally synchronized. Method names, formatting tokens (e.g. `YYYY-MM-DD`, `dddd`), fiscal year quarters, and edge case handling should match across all implementations."
  }, {
    "heading": "core-contribution-principles",
    "content": "**Certified Range Accuracy (1976 – 2100 BS)**:\nAny changes affecting date conversion or calendar math must pass the exhaustive ephemeris verification tests covering 1976/01/01 to 2100/12/31 BS."
  }, {
    "heading": "core-contribution-principles",
    "content": "**Deterministic Timezone Isolation**:\nDate arithmetic, weekday getters, and day start/end calculations must execute deterministically regardless of the host machine's local timezone."
  }, {
    "heading": "development-environment-setup",
    "content": "Select your target language below for environment setup and test commands:"
  }, {
    "heading": "nodejs--typescript-setup",
    "content": "**Prerequisites**: Node.js `>= 22.0.0`, pnpm `>= 10.0.0`"
  }, {
    "heading": "python-setup",
    "content": "**Prerequisites**: Python `>= 3.9`, uv (recommended)"
  }, {
    "heading": "php-setup",
    "content": "**Prerequisites**: PHP `>= 7.1`, Composer"
  }, {
    "heading": "documentation-engine-setup",
    "content": "**Prerequisites**: Node.js `>= 22.0.0`, pnpm `>= 10.0.0`"
  }, {
    "heading": "documentation-engine-setup",
    "content": "Open http://localhost:3000 to view local live edits with instant hot reload."
  }, {
    "heading": "pull-request-guidelines",
    "content": "**Fork & Branch**: Fork the target repository and create a descriptive branch:"
  }, {
    "heading": "pull-request-guidelines",
    "content": "**Write Tests**: Accompany every bug fix or feature with clear unit tests verifying the behavior."
  }, {
    "heading": "pull-request-guidelines",
    "content": "**Run CI Checks**: Verify that all test suites, linters, and type checkers pass without errors."
  }, {
    "heading": "pull-request-guidelines",
    "content": "**Descriptive Commits**: Use conventional commits (e.g., `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`)."
  }, {
    "heading": "pull-request-guidelines",
    "content": "**Submit PR**: Open a Pull Request referencing any related issues with reproduction steps or rationale."
  }, {
    "heading": "community--code-of-conduct",
