    "heading": "timezone-drift-prevention",
    "content": "One of the most frequent bugs when converting dates in distributed environments is **single-day shifting caused by local server timezones**."
  }, {
    "heading": "timezone-drift-prevention",
    "content": "For example, parsing `\"2024-11-01\"` using `new Date(\"2024-11-01\")` in a system running in UTC-5 (Eastern Time) produces `2024-10-31 19:00:00`, which erroneously converts to the previous Nepali date."
  }, {
    "heading": "timezone-drift-prevention",
    "content": "`ADtoBS` and `BStoAD` internally enforce **strict UTC parsing** via `Date.UTC`:"
